\details{
The degree assortativity coefficient is defined as the Pearson correlation
coefficient between the degrees of nodes at either end of each edge
(Newman 2002):

\deqn{r = \frac{\sum_{jk} jk(e_{jk} - q_j q_k)}{\sigma_q^2}}

